  "diagnostic_method": "Independently reconstruct the public endpoint path, fixed elbow branch and exact marker-derived source lengths. Compose the original complete RGBA parts with bicubic inverse rigid maps using source/destination pixel-center correction. Compare every producer RGB PNG directly to that independent construction. Source-color centroids use the supplied marker colors within11px of each known target and max-channel color distance15, before and after encoding. Centroids are descriptive diagnostics, not a new official detector or scoring rule.",
  "sampling_and_codec_caveat": "The producer uses a conventional +0.5 pixel-center correction. The index-based reference and pixel-center composition differ by at most0.9914px of rigid sampling phase, within the disclosed2px source and3px physical allowances. Tiny high-contrast7px marker supports, integer-only alignment and yuv420p sampling may be sensitive to this phase. This audit does not isolate an exact codec/reference cause or replace the frozen numeric rule.",
  "manual_visual_observation": "Both complete patterned links remain rigid and connected; the fixed ground and moving tip follow the source-defined geometry throughout all36 native frames. No >3px joint/endpoint displacement, repainting, stretching, missing part or visible branch flip was established. The small marker raster differences do not by themselves establish an actual media defect.",
